    "title": "Trump reveals the next target of the Doge of Elon Musk, while mass cutbacks on the government continue",
    "text": "By Katelyn Caralle, senior American political reporter in Washington, DC\nPublished: 15:24 GMT, February 9, 2025 | Updated: 15:28 GMT, February 9, 2025\nThe next target of Elon Musk: the Ministry of Education.\nPresident Donald Trump says that he will instruct the head of his Department of Government Efficiency (Doge) to investigate the education department in potential cuts.\n“I have to run on this and people want me to find this,” Trump told Fox News-Gastheer Bret Baier in a pre-gave interview that is broadcast for the Super Bowl on Sunday afternoon.\nTrump said he fully trusts Elon to find fraud and identify where government spending can be reduced if he tries to reduce our waste and climbing debt.\nIt comes after USAID was completely closed last week by Musk and Trump.\nThe Tesla and SpaceX billionaire also said this weekend that the estimate of ‘unambiguous and clear fraud’ at the Ministry of Finance is $ 1 billion every week.\n“I’m going to tell him very quickly, as perhaps in 24 hours, to check the Ministry of Education – he will find the same thing,” Trump said about the next Project of Musk.\n“Then I go to the Army Laten we check the army,” added the supreme commander. ‘We are going to find billions, hundreds of billions of dollars in fraud and abuse. And you know, people have chosen me about that. ‘\nThis story breaks and will be updated\nDonald Trump sat down with Bret Baier for an interview broadcast on FOX News on Sunday for the Super Bowl\nShare or comment on this article: Trump reveals the following target of the Doge of Elon Musk as a massive cuts on the government\n(Tagstotranslate) DailyMail",
